          "Chocolate is today one of the most widely enjoyed foods on Earth, yet its origins lie in the ancient civilisations of Central America. There, more than three thousand years ago, people learned to harvest the beans of the cacao tree, a small tree that grows in the warm, shaded conditions of the tropical forest. The beans were not eaten as we eat chocolate now. Instead, they were roasted, ground, and mixed with water and spices to make a bitter, frothy drink that bore little resemblance to the sweet confection familiar to modern consumers.",
